# the aarch64 catalog
#
# the rows, their codec and decode dispatch are generated by gen aarch64 from
# the instruction model (Instructions.json of the AARCHMRS release vendored
# under gen/vendor/aarchmrs), which states every encoding's bits, assembly
# symbols and feature conditions, and the overlay under gen/data/aarch64, which
# states what the model leaves out: what each symbol is as an operand, under
# which value of streaming each group exists, which rows are data independent
# time, and what each instruction does beyond its operands. the field kinds,
# extension catalog and register file are their own modules. the tests here walk
# the shipped rows: every row encodes and decodes back to itself, every row's
# effect is complete, and the rows of sve, sme and dit read the state the way
# the manual states it.

use A: std.allocator;

fwd masc.isa.aarch64.gen_row.CODEC;
